WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.200
Digital Forensics and Incident Response helps organizations understand incidents, preserve evidence, respond safely, and improve resilience.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.140
Digital forensics gives the team a reliable way to collect and analyze evidence.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:21.040
Incident response gives the organization a structured way to contain harm, coordinate decisions, recover services, and communicate clearly.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.220
Together, they turn uncertainty into informed action.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.520
Strong DFIR depends on preparation.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:33.860
Plans, roles, access, tools, logging, and procedures should exist before the incident begins.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:40.800
During detection and analysis, teams build a timeline from evidence and separate confirmed facts from assumptions.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.900
During containment, they limit damage while protecting important evidence whenever possible.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:53.880
During eradication and recovery, they remove the cause of compromise, restore systems, and validate that operations can safely resume.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.500
Evidence handling is a recurring theme.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:08.640
Logs, disk images, memory captures, network data, cloud records, screenshots, and notes can all matter, but they are most valuable when collected carefully and documented well.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:16.380
Chain of custody, preservation decisions, and clear notes help future reviewers understand what happened and how the organization responded.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.160
The goal of DFIR is not only to find what happened.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.860
The larger goal is to help the organization make safe, informed decisions.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:30.000
That includes technical decisions, legal decisions, operational decisions, and business decisions.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:38.140
A mature DFIR practice reduces immediate harm, improves future defenses, and gives leadership a clearer view of risk when the stakes are high.
